        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "884715de-760a-53fc-a071-f34d459392e3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rosemary Willis, John F. Kennedy\n- Places: Dealey Plaza, downtown Dallas, Texas, West End district\n- Events: Assassination of John F. Kennedy, Zapruder film\n\nFacts:\n- On November 22, 1963, Dealey Plaza in the historic West End district of downtown Dallas, Texas, was the location of the assassination of John F. Kennedy.\n- At the start of the assassination, Rosemary Willis is clearly visible in the Zapruder film wearing a white hooded coat and a red skirt.\n- In Dealey Plaza, Rosemary Willis trotted on the grass to the left of the presidential limousine and ran southwestward parallel with the limousine.\n- For a short time in Dealey Plaza, Rosemary Willis faced the presidential limousine when it was directly to her right.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
